# Patterns for scan-proprietary.sh — one ERE per line, matched case-insensitively.
#
# Copy this file to patterns.local and replace the placeholders with the
# identifiers specific to YOUR migration project. patterns.local is
# gitignored, so the vocabulary you search for never reaches the repository.
#
#     cp patterns.example patterns.local
#     $EDITOR patterns.local
#     ./scan-proprietary.sh
#
# What belongs here:
#   - usernames, machine names and absolute paths from the migration host
#   - the project directory name
#   - source library / member prefixes on the IBM i side
#   - copybook naming conventions specific to the customer
#   - database / schema names
#   - the customer's own name and product names
#
# Examples of the SHAPE (deliberately generic — replace them):

# host user and project directory
# ^myusername$
# MyProjectDir

# IBM i source library prefixes
# [a-z]+src_cobol
# [A-Z]{2}_P_CPY

# database and schema names
# myappdb
# myapp_schema

# customer and product names
# acmecorp
# acme-billing
